WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.032
The school Week Three stations require peripheral IV and tibial IO practice. Learn them as clinical decisions followed by technical steps, not a race to place a catheter in every patient.
学校第3周站点要求练习外周静脉及胫骨骨内通路。要先作临床决策，再完成技术步骤，而不是比赛给每位患者置管。

00:00:13.032 --> 00:00:26.880
This lecture teaches the whole sequence and the reasons behind it. The exact school catheter, drill, checkoff form and original PCP One Ten/One Twenty slide bodies remain source gaps.
本课教授完整流程及原因。学校实际导管、钻具、技能评分表，以及PCP 110和120原始幻灯片正文，仍未取得。

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:37.248
Device examples are clearly identified as manufacturer examples. They do not prove which product the school uses or replace supervised hands-on feedback.
本课明确标注制造商器材示例。它们不能证明学校使用哪个产品，也不能替代有督导的实际操作反馈。

00:00:37.248 --> 00:00:48.024
Keep necessary airway, breathing and circulation support continuous. An invasive access attempt must not delay more important treatment or conveyance.
应持续进行必要的气道、呼吸及循环支持。侵入性通路尝试不能延误更重要的治疗或转运。

00:00:48.024 --> 00:01:00.792
Start by stating what the route will deliver or enable in the current plan. A technically easy vein is not an indication, and a person being conveyed to hospital does not automatically need a field IV.
先说明通路在当前方案中要给什么，或支持什么治疗。静脉好扎不是适应证，转运去医院也不代表一定需要院前IV。

00:01:00.792 --> 00:01:13.968
Consider whether an appropriate less invasive route can meet the treatment need. The choice depends on the actual patient, medicine and authorized pathway, not a general belief that IV is always better.
考虑合适的低侵入途径能否满足需要。选择应依据实际患者、药物和获准路径，而不是笼统认为IV总是更好。

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:26.064
A specific pathway or an anticipated treatment by an intercepting advanced clinician may justify access. State the real reason instead of using keep-vein-open as a default explanation.
特定路径要求，或即将会合的高级人员预计要实施的治疗，可能构成置管理由。要说真实原因，不能默认用保持静脉通畅解释。

00:01:26.064 --> 00:01:36.384
Balance benefit with pain, contamination, bleeding, infiltration and delay. The access decision is revisited if the treatment plan changes.
收益要与疼痛、污染、出血、渗漏和延误相权衡。治疗方案改变时，也应重新考虑通路决策。

00:01:36.384 --> 00:01:45.168
The assigned PR twenty-six uses JAY to examine the access decision. Justifiable asks whether the intended care actually needs it.
指定PR26用JAY审视通路决策。Justifiable问的是：拟进行的照护是否确实需要这条通路。

00:01:45.168 --> 00:01:56.856
Accountable asks whether the decision is defensible and whether you accept responsibility for consequences. You asks you to consider the patient's experience of benefit, burden and dignity.
Accountable问决定是否有据，以及你是否承担后果；You则要求换位思考患者的收益、负担和尊严。

00:01:56.856 --> 00:02:08.736
Consent to an unnecessary stick does not by itself make it appropriate clinical care. Skill maintenance belongs on simulation equipment and through the proper educational process.
患者同意一次不必要穿刺，本身不能让它成为适当临床照护。维持技能应使用模拟器材并经过正规教育流程。

00:02:08.736 --> 00:02:19.176
In a station, say the indication and a reason you would stop. That makes your decision observable rather than hiding it behind a successful needle placement.
站点中要说出适应证和一个停止理由，让决策可观察，而不是把它藏在最终成功置管之后。

00:02:19.176 --> 00:02:30.864
The school teaches procedures that may have additional licence, endorsement, service or supervision conditions. Completing this lecture alone does not satisfy those conditions.
学校教授的操作可能另有执照、附加资格、机构或督导条件。仅完成本课不能满足这些条件。

00:02:30.864 --> 00:02:42.000
Current D three prohibits PCP cannulation under age twelve by any method. IO has further restrictions that we will separate from the broader manufacturer instructions.
当前D03禁止PCP以任何方法给未满12岁者置管。IO还有额外限制，必须与制造商较宽泛说明分开。

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:53.880
Use the school model for practice until the actual required education and authorization apply. Do not generalize a hospital nursing description or a vendor age range into local permission.
实际教育和授权条件未满足前，应在学校模型上练习。不能把医院护理描述或厂商年龄范围直接当作本地权限。

00:02:53.880 --> 00:03:05.712
Confirm competence with the actual device and the relevant patient group. If uncertain, maintain support, seek the required guidance and choose an authorized alternative.
须确认已掌握具体器材及相关患者群体。不确定时应维持支持、寻求规定指导，并选择获准替代方案。

00:03:05.712 --> 00:03:16.344
An IV puts the selected solution into the vascular system without tissue absorption. What happens afterward depends on its composition and the patient's physiology.
IV把所选液体直接送入血管系统，不需先经组织吸收；之后的作用取决于液体组成和患者生理状态。

00:03:16.344 --> 00:03:27.096
Water and dissolved particles distribute across compartments differently. A volume entering the vein is not necessarily the same amount remaining in plasma over time.
水和溶解颗粒在不同区室中的分布不同。进入静脉的量，不一定等于一段时间后仍留在血浆中的量。

00:03:27.096 --> 00:03:38.328
Blood pressure is one part of perfusion assessment, not a complete measure of tissue flow. A small pressure rise with worsening breathing can represent harm rather than success.
血压只是灌注评估的一部分，不是组织血流的完整测量。血压略升但呼吸恶化，可能代表伤害而非成功。

00:03:38.328 --> 00:03:51.216
State an expected physiological endpoint and watch for both benefit and overload. Later reading develops hydrostatic and osmotic mechanisms rather than using a simple fill-the-tank slogan.
要说明预期生理终点，同时观察获益及容量过负荷。后续阅读会解释静水压和渗透机制，不能只套用加满水箱的口号。

00:03:51.216 --> 00:04:03.168
Before the attempt, assess the reason for access and the current primary priorities. Identify relevant losses, actual intake, medicines and previous response where available.
尝试前先评通路理由及当前初评优先问题。可行时了解相关丢失量、实际摄入、药物和此前治疗反应。

00:04:03.168 --> 00:04:13.512
Record useful baseline observations and symptoms, including respiratory status and perfusion. They give meaning to the response after fluid or medicine.
记录有用的基线观察及症状，包括呼吸状态和灌注。这些资料让补液或给药后的反应有意义。

00:04:13.512 --> 00:04:25.272
Ask about relevant allergy, difficult access, dialysis access, local injury and prior problems. Explain the proposed route and obtain the appropriate consent.
询问相关过敏、困难通路、透析通路、局部损伤及既往问题。解释拟用通路，并取得适当同意。

00:04:25.272 --> 00:04:35.784
Decide who maintains patient support while another person prepares. Record a reassessment trigger and an escalation plan before repeated attempts consume attention.
明确另一人准备时由谁维持患者支持。反复尝试占据注意力前，要先定复评触发点及升级方案。

00:04:35.784 --> 00:04:47.784
Inspect and palpate before committing to a site. A useful vein is not just blue or visible; its course, depth and condition must suit the intended catheter and therapy.
决定部位前先看并触诊。适合的静脉不只是蓝色或可见，其走向、深度和状态都要适合导管及治疗。

00:04:47.784 --> 00:04:58.992
Assess a soft, compressible, nonpulsatile segment using the trained method. An artery, tendon or scar can be misidentified if you depend only on appearance.
按受训方法寻找柔软、可压、无搏动的一段。只凭外观，可能把动脉、肌腱或瘢痕认错。

00:04:58.992 --> 00:05:09.792
Look for a segment with enough usable course and avoid injured, infected or obviously compromised tissue. Patient comfort and limb function also matter.
应有足够可用走向，并避开受伤、感染或明显受损组织。患者舒适及肢体功能也要考虑。

00:05:09.792 --> 00:05:20.832
When volume depletion makes veins difficult, do not repeatedly probe the same area. Reassess the need, equipment, help and actual escalation options.
容量不足使静脉难找时，不能反复在同一区域探刺。应重评需要、器材、协助及真实升级选择。

00:05:20.832 --> 00:05:31.872
Starting distally can preserve future options when the vein and therapy are suitable. It is not an absolute command to use a poor hand vein for every urgent treatment.
静脉及治疗合适时，从较远端开始可保留后续选择；但这不代表紧急治疗一律必须使用条件差的手背静脉。

00:05:31.872 --> 00:05:44.064
Catheter length, vein size, expected movement and the required therapy affect selection. A site at a flexion point may obstruct or become uncomfortable during transport.
导管长度、静脉大小、预计移动及治疗需求都会影响选点。关节屈曲处在转运中可能受阻或引起不适。

00:05:44.064 --> 00:05:57.096
Protect an arteriovenous fistula or graft and assess local infection, trauma, edema and relevant prior procedures. Resolve uncertainty through the actual policy and clinical plan.
应保护动静脉瘘或移植物，并评局部感染、创伤、水肿及相关既往操作。不确定时须依实际政策及照护方案解决。

00:05:57.096 --> 00:06:08.064
Specific pathways can add considerations, such as preserving access for an anticipated coronary procedure. Do not let an ideal-site search create a conveyance delay.
特定路径还可能要求为预期冠脉操作保留通路。但不能为了寻找理想位置而延误转运。

00:06:08.064 --> 00:06:18.648
Choose a suitable catheter for the vein, patient and therapy. A larger bore can support greater flow but may increase local trauma if poorly matched.
应按静脉、患者和治疗选择合适导管。较粗内径可支持较大流量，但匹配不当会增加局部损伤。

00:06:18.648 --> 00:06:29.664
Flow depends on more than gauge: length, connectors, tubing, pressure and resistance all matter. Do not assume a colour alone proves capacity or suitability.
流量不只取决于规格，还受长度、接头、管路、压力及阻力影响。不能只凭颜色判断容量或适用性。

00:06:29.664 --> 00:06:39.360
A steel collection needle and a flexible over-the-needle catheter leave different things in the patient. Identify exactly what you are handling before beginning.
钢制采血针与套在针上的柔性导管，留在患者体内的部分不同。开始前必须认清手中器材。

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:50.880
Blood-control and needle-safety mechanisms are product-specific. Practise the actual model; do not blend a previous device's hand motions into an unfamiliar catheter.
止血及针安全机制因产品而异。应练实际型号，不能把旧器材手法拼到陌生导管上。

00:06:50.880 --> 00:07:00.840
Gather the full setup and inspect packaging, expiry and integrity. Put the sharps container within the appropriate safe working position before beginning.
备齐整套器材，检查包装、有效期及完整性。开始前把锐器盒放在安全且适当的工作位置。

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:12.864
Prepare the selected catheter, site-cleansing material and venous tourniquet. Prepare a primed compatible connector and the prescribed solution or flush using the actual equipment.
备好所选导管、皮肤消毒用品及静脉止血带；按实际器材准备已预充的相容接头，以及规定液体或冲管液。

00:07:12.864 --> 00:07:22.704
Have the dressing and securement ready so a successful catheter is not left unsupported while someone searches for tape. Keep critical parts protected.
敷料及固定用品要预先备好，避免置管成功后无人稳定导管、却还在找胶带。关键部位应持续受保护。

00:07:22.704 --> 00:07:34.104
Make a plan for a failed attempt and for patient deterioration. Preparation is a safety step that reduces interruption, contamination and uncontrolled sharps handling.
要预想失败和患者恶化的处理。准备本身就是安全步骤，可减少中断、污染及失控锐器操作。

00:07:34.104 --> 00:07:45.792
Aseptic continuity is not one alcohol wipe at the beginning. The skin, catheter, extension and access surfaces must remain appropriately protected throughout the sequence.
无菌连续性不是开始时擦一次酒精。皮肤、导管、延长管及入口表面，都须在全过程得到适当保护。

00:07:45.792 --> 00:07:56.280
Apply the approved antiseptic with the specified contact and drying time. Re-palpating prepared skin with a contaminated finger breaks the intended barrier.
使用获准消毒剂，并完成规定接触及干燥时间。用被污染手指再触已消毒皮肤，会破坏预期屏障。

00:07:56.280 --> 00:08:08.208
Protect critical parts when opening, connecting and securing. Gloves do not make a touched sterile surface clean, and a connector called needleless still needs correct aseptic access.
开包、连接和固定时要保护关键部位。戴手套不会让摸过的无菌面重新干净；无针接头仍需正确无菌连接。

00:08:08.208 --> 00:08:19.872
If contamination occurs, identify it and restore the barrier using the actual trained method. Do not hide a break because the time target or a partner's expectation feels urgent.
污染发生时要明确指出，并按真实受训方法恢复屏障。不能因为计时或同伴催促，就掩盖操作中断点。

00:08:19.872 --> 00:08:32.568
In supervised model practice, stabilize the limb and site and follow the device's insertion method. The exact angle and advancement are not universal across products and tissue depths.
模型督导练习中，应稳定肢体和部位，遵器材插入方法。角度及推进量并不适用于所有产品和组织深度。

00:08:32.568 --> 00:08:43.920
Blood return can show needle entry without proving that the flexible catheter tip is fully within the vein. Some devices have separate needle and catheter flashback cues.
回血可表示针尖进入，但不能证明柔性导管末端已完全在静脉内。有些产品分别提供针和导管的回血提示。

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:55.776
The manufacturer example in the source notes illustrates that distinction; it is not evidence the school uses that catheter. Ask the instructor to demonstrate the actual product's transitions.
来源中的制造商例子用于解释这个区别，并不能证明学校使用该导管。应请教师示范实际产品各转换步骤。

00:08:55.776 --> 00:09:08.208
Maintain control and do not fish blindly. If the expected cue is absent or the patient has concerning pain, stop and reassess rather than forcing a successful-looking result.
须保持控制，不能盲目探刺。预期提示未出现，或患者出现令人担忧的疼痛时，应停下重评，不能硬做出成功外观。

00:09:08.208 --> 00:09:21.624
Once appropriate entry is confirmed, advance the flexible catheter using the actual trained device method. Do not assume every catheter uses the same flashback chamber or withdrawal sequence.
确认适当进入后，按实际受训器材方法推进柔性导管。不能假定所有导管的回血腔和退针顺序相同。

00:09:21.624 --> 00:09:30.120
Never reinsert a withdrawn needle into the catheter. It can damage or shear the catheter and create an embolic complication.
绝不能把已退出的针重新插回导管，这可能损伤或切断导管，造成栓塞并发症。

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:42.192
Release the venous tourniquet as required, stabilize the catheter and remove the needle using its intended safety mechanism. Avoid uncontrolled bending or a loose exposed sharp.
按要求松开止血带，稳定导管，并使用原有安全机制退针。避免失控弯折或留下暴露锐器。

00:09:42.192 --> 00:09:52.992
Connect promptly with protected compatible parts and secure the route. Product-specific blood control does not excuse leaving a hub open or touching critical surfaces.
应及时用受保护、相容部件连接并固定。产品有止血功能，不代表可以让接头敞开或触碰关键表面。

00:09:52.992 --> 00:10:05.448
If cannulation fails, use the actual safe removal sequence and manage the site. Inspect the device and control bleeding, especially when the patient has an increased bleeding risk.
置管失败时，按实际器材的安全退出顺序处理局部。应检查器材并止血，尤其注意出血风险增加者。

00:10:05.448 --> 00:10:14.376
Do not reuse a catheter or needle, repeatedly probe damaged tissue or reinsert a steel needle into a partly withdrawn plastic catheter.
不能重用导管或针，不能在受损组织反复探刺，也不能把钢针插回部分退出的塑料导管。

00:10:14.376 --> 00:10:25.416
Record attempts according to the actual policy and include colleagues' attempts in collective limits when specified. An unsuccessful stick is not erased by later success.
按真实政策记录尝试次数；若规定集体上限，要包括同事次数。后来成功不能抹去先前失败。

00:10:25.416 --> 00:10:37.176
Reassess the current need and conveyance priorities. Two missed IVs do not independently authorize IO in a conscious dehydrated patient; its separate conditions must be met.
应重评当前需要及转运优先级。清醒脱水者两次IV失败，不会单独授权IO，仍须满足其独立条件。

00:10:37.176 --> 00:10:46.776
Before using the route, inspect the site and ask about discomfort if possible. Trace the connection all the way from the intended solution to the patient.
使用前检查局部，可行时询问不适，并从目标液体一直追踪连接到患者。

00:10:46.776 --> 00:10:58.920
Assess according to the actual catheter/therapy method. Neither a previous flashback nor a momentary easy flush proves that future delivery will remain intravascular.
应按真实导管及治疗方法评估。先前回血或短暂轻松冲管，都不能证明以后始终会在血管内给入。

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:09.384
Resistance, new pain, swelling or leakage is not a reason to use greater force. Stop and evaluate the cause and the patient before proceeding.
阻力、新疼痛、肿胀或渗漏，不能靠更大推力解决。继续前应停下，检查原因及患者。

00:11:09.384 --> 00:11:18.576
Recheck after repositioning and during delivery. A route that was satisfactory before lifting the patient can be displaced or kinked afterward.
改变体位后及给入中都要再查。搬患者前合格的通路，搬动后可能已经移位或折曲。

00:11:18.576 --> 00:11:29.160
Use the intended securement to reduce motion and catheter migration. Stabilize the extension so a cable tug does not pull directly on the insertion site.
使用规定固定装置，减少移动和导管移位。延长管也要稳定，避免线路牵拉直接作用于穿刺点。

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:39.048
Keep the site assessable with the approved dressing. A thick wrap that hides tissue swelling can delay recognition of infiltration or extravasation.
获准敷料应允许评估局部。厚包扎若遮住组织肿胀，可能延迟识别渗漏或外渗。

00:11:39.048 --> 00:11:48.624
Do not constrict the limb or obscure distal circulation. Check comfort and function, and label the required device and insertion details.
不能勒紧肢体或遮挡远端循环评估。要检查舒适及功能，并标注规定的器材和置入资料。

00:11:48.624 --> 00:12:00.384
After every transfer, reassess the patient, site and complete route rather than only looking at the fluid bag. Securement success is demonstrated by continued safe function.
每次转移后应复评患者、局部和整条通路，不能只看液袋。持续安全有效，才证明固定成功。

00:12:00.384 --> 00:12:11.520
This original arithmetic example uses a simulation order of one hundred millilitres over twenty minutes. That equals five millilitres per minute or three hundred per hour.
原创算术示例采用模拟医嘱：100毫升在20分钟内给入，相当于每分钟5毫升，或每小时300毫升。

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:23.136
With a training set explicitly labelled fifteen drops per millilitre, multiply five by fifteen to obtain seventy-five drops per minute. A different set changes that answer.
若训练输液器明确标为15滴每毫升，5乘15得到每分钟75滴。换一种滴系数，结果就会改变。

00:12:23.136 --> 00:12:35.400
Read the actual drop factor and verify the device programming or gravity delivery. No universal drop volume exists, and setting a rate does not prove that the intended amount reached the vein.
要读真实滴系数，并核器材设置或重力送入。不存在通用每滴体积；设置正确也不能证明目标量已进入静脉。

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:45.744
This is not a clinical fluid prescription. In care, actual indication, limits, delivered amount, response and local instructions govern the plan.
这不是临床补液处方。照护中须按真实适应证、限制、实际量、反应和本地要求制定方案。

00:12:45.744 --> 00:13:16.008
The school also assigns a BD single-port closed-catheter demonstration. Its actual product name is Nexiva. The bilingual guide now follows the complete available narrative, separating needle entry, catheter advancement, safe needle withdrawal and the later clamp-and-connection sequence. Initial blood flash does not by itself prove a correctly positioned, patent catheter. Do not apply one model’s grip, push-tab or vent-plug instructions to a different device.
学校另指定BD单口闭合导管示范，实际产品名称为Nexiva。中英指南现跟随完整可取得叙述，区分针进入、送管、安全撤针及之后夹闭连接顺序。初次回血本身，不证明导管正确定位或通畅。不能把一种型号的握柄、推片或排气塞说明，套给另一器械。

00:13:16.008 --> 00:13:46.008
Use the video with the existing supervised vascular-access sequence: consent, the actual indication, aseptic preparation, safe handling, securement and verification of delivery and response. The linked historical six-rights article adds concentration and documentation checks, but it does not replace the school’s expanded medication framework. A named device and a completed checklist are not proof that the patient received the intended treatment safely.
应把视频连接现有受监督血管通路流程：同意、真实指征、无菌准备、安全处理、固定，以及核实给入和反应。链接历史六项文章补充浓度及记录核对，但不替代学校扩展用药框架。器械有名称、清单已打勾，都不证明患者已安全收到预期治疗。

00:13:46.008 --> 00:13:56.688
Verify the solution and actual indication rather than using fluids as an automatic response to every low pressure. Different causes of shock require different priorities.
应核液体和真实适应证，不能所有低血压都自动补液。不同休克原因有不同优先事项。

00:13:56.688 --> 00:14:07.608
Current D three includes fluid reassessment and a consultation requirement when more than two litres is anticipated. That is not a target to give two litres to everyone.
当前D03要求复评补液，预计超过两升时须咨询；这不是要求每个人都补到两升。

00:14:07.608 --> 00:14:18.792
Use the actual age, pathway and clinical condition for bolus decisions. Do not turn an adult or hospital example into an unrestricted pediatric PCP instruction.
液体冲击决策须依据真实年龄、路径和病情。不能把成人或医院例子当作不受限的儿科PCP指令。

00:14:18.792 --> 00:14:31.008
Watch breathing as well as pressure and perfusion. If new respiratory distress appears, stop automatic escalation, reassess the patient and obtain the appropriate plan.
呼吸与血压、灌注都要观察。若出现新呼吸窘迫，应停止自动加量，重评患者并取得合适方案。

00:14:31.008 --> 00:14:40.920
Reassess after each delivered intervention, not only after a bag is empty. Compare the patient with the baseline and the endpoint you stated.
每次干预实际给入后都要复评，不能等袋空。应与基线及预先说明的治疗终点比较。

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:52.656
Ask what changed: awareness, symptoms, pulse/pressure, breathing and local access findings. Then ask whether the expected benefit actually occurred.
先问什么变了：意识、症状、脉搏血压、呼吸及局部通路；再问预期益处是否真的出现。

00:14:52.656 --> 00:15:02.568
Ask what got worse. A pressure rise accompanied by new crackles or an increasing oxygen requirement is not an uncomplicated success.
还要问什么更糟。血压上升却新出现湿啰音或氧需求增加，不算没有并发症的成功。

00:15:02.568 --> 00:15:11.712
Use the answer to update the plan with the appropriate authority. Do not keep the original infusion running by habit while deterioration accumulates.
应在相应权限下根据答案更新方案。不能恶化不断累积时，还习惯性维持原输注。

00:15:11.712 --> 00:15:23.544
Local pain, swelling, blanching, leakage or altered distal function requires prompt assessment. An infusion can continue into tissue even without a pump alarm.
局部痛、肿、苍白、渗漏或远端功能改变，需要迅速评估。即使泵未报警，也可能继续向组织输注。

00:15:23.544 --> 00:15:36.072
For suspected extravasation, do not flush. Preserve or remove the device according to the actual product-specific management plan rather than automatically applying a generic removal rule.
疑似外渗不能冲管。应按实际制剂的专门处理方案决定保留还是移除器材，不能自动套用通用拔除规则。

00:15:36.072 --> 00:15:49.368
Systemic breathlessness, collapse or new instability needs immediate patient assessment and support. Do not assume every problem near an IV has the same cause or the same positioning solution.
全身气促、倒下或新不稳定，需要立即评估并支持患者。不能假定IV附近出现的问题都有同一原因或相同体位处理。

00:15:49.368 --> 00:16:01.488
Communicate exact product, concentration, amount, rate, timing and site findings. Document both the clinical care and the required incident process truthfully.
须准确交代产品、浓度、量、速度、时间和局部所见，并如实完成临床记录及规定事件流程。

00:16:01.488 --> 00:16:11.616
An intraosseous device provides access to the medullary vascular space. It can enable indicated therapy when the actual conditions for IO are met.
骨内器材提供骨髓血管空间通路。满足真实IO条件时，可经此实施有指征的治疗。

00:16:11.616 --> 00:16:22.416
A device brochure may list multiple sites and ages. Local PCP permission is narrower and must be checked separately from what the product is technically designed to do.
器材宣传资料可能列多个部位和年龄。本地PCP权限更窄，应与产品技术上能做什么分别核对。

00:16:22.416 --> 00:16:34.152
Insertion and infusion can cause different pain, and malposition can cause serious tissue injury. A catheter standing in bone is not proof that its tip or flow is correct.
置入和输注可引起不同疼痛，位置错误可造成严重组织损伤。导管立在骨上，不能证明末端或流动正确。

00:16:34.152 --> 00:16:46.032
Do not let access placement impair airway support, high-quality compressions or defibrillation during arrest. Route creation supports the care plan rather than becoming its main event.
骤停时，建立通路不能妨碍气道支持、高质量按压及除颤。通路应支持照护方案，而不是变成主角。

00:16:46.032 --> 00:17:03.432
Current PR twelve requires the relevant PCP scope-expansion education. Its restricted arrest branch concerns patients twelve or older with clear hypovolemia and fluids critical to the resuscitation plan, after the specified peripheral-access failure or unavailability.
当前PR12要求PCP相关扩展范围教育。其受限骤停支针对至少12岁、明确低血容量且补液对复苏至关重要者，并须满足所列外周通路失败或不可用条件。

00:17:03.432 --> 00:17:15.576
The page also permits placement under direct supervision of an on-scene ACP or higher. A telephone conversation is not automatically the same thing as that specified supervision.
页面另允许在现场ACP或以上人员直接督导下置入。电话交谈不自动等于该规定现场督导。

00:17:15.576 --> 00:17:28.104
PCP use is tibial only and limited to two collective attempts per patient. A failed or dislodged site must not be re-cannulated, and the stated under-twelve restriction remains.
PCP只可使用胫骨，且每位患者集体最多两次。失败或脱出部位不可重新置管，未满12岁的限制仍然适用。

00:17:28.104 --> 00:17:43.272
Therefore, an awake vomiting patient with difficult IV access is not an independent PCP IO indication merely because two attempts failed. The school case needs an authorized escalation/supervision decision.
因此，清醒呕吐且IV困难者，不能仅因两次失败就成为PCP独立IO适应证。学校案例需要获准的升级及督导决定。

00:17:43.272 --> 00:17:55.080
Check the intended limb for trauma, local tissue damage, infection, relevant surgery and joint replacement. Do not choose a convenient-looking point without a full site check.
应检查目标肢体有无创伤、局部组织损坏、感染、相关手术及关节置换。不能只凭位置看起来方便就选择。

00:17:55.080 --> 00:18:05.136
Current PR twelve includes recent same-site placement within forty-eight hours as a contraindication. Document known prior attempts and their locations.
当前PR12把48小时内近期同部位置入列为禁忌。应记录已知先前尝试及其位置。

00:18:05.136 --> 00:18:16.200
If landmarks cannot be identified reliably, the site is not made safe by estimating a fixed distance on the skin. Obtain the appropriate alternative plan and help.
无法可靠辨认标志时，估计皮肤上固定距离也不能让部位变安全。应取得适当替代方案及协助。

00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:26.448
Count all collective attempts and preserve circulation and function. Site screening is part of the clinical safety decision, not a formality after drilling.
应计算所有集体尝试，并保护循环和功能。部位筛查是临床安全决策的一部分，不是钻后补手续。

00:18:26.448 --> 00:18:35.760
For the adult proximal-tibial manufacturer example, support and extend the leg and palpate the actual patella and tibial tuberosity.
成人近端胫骨制造商示例要求支撑并伸直腿，触认真实髌骨和胫骨粗隆。

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:49.680
The cited adult guide locates a point about two centimetres medial to the tuberosity on the flat tibial surface. This is a relational landmark, not permission to drill any two-centimetre skin estimate.
所引成人指南在胫骨平面上，定位于粗隆内侧约两厘米。这是相对解剖标志，不是任估皮肤两厘米就可钻入。

00:18:49.680 --> 00:19:02.448
Confirm the anatomy, absence of contraindications and the actual local taught site with an instructor on the model. Do not import the brochure's pediatric or humeral sites into PCP permission.
应与教师在模型上确认解剖、排除禁忌，并核本地实际所教位置。不能把宣传册儿童或肱骨部位变成PCP权限。

00:19:02.448 --> 00:19:11.568
Landmarking must be checked before insertion. A figure or verbal description cannot demonstrate that your fingers have located the correct structure.
定位必须在插入前核实。图或口头描述，不能证明你的手指真的找到了正确结构。

00:19:11.568 --> 00:19:23.232
Prepare the actual device and suitable needle set, primed extension, stabilization equipment and therapy plan. Check packaging and the driver before contacting the patient.
应备实际器材、合适针组、预充延长管、固定用品及治疗方案；接触患者前先查包装和驱动器。

00:19:23.232 --> 00:19:37.248
Needle length must account for tissue depth. The cited EZ-IO guide requires the specified length marking to remain visible at bone contact before powered insertion; colour or body weight alone is not enough.
针长必须考虑组织深度。所引EZ-IO指南要求在接触骨面、尚未电动推进前，规定长度标记仍可见；仅凭颜色或体重不够。

00:19:37.248 --> 00:19:47.712
Use the actual trained angle and controlled gentle technique, not excessive force. Do not invent a depth or keep drilling after the expected insertion endpoint.
应采用真实受训角度及轻柔受控技术，不能过度用力。不能自定深度，或达到预期置入终点后继续钻。

00:19:47.712 --> 00:19:59.640
Stabilize the device while removing the driver and stylet as trained, immediately contain the sharp and use a protected primed connection. A generic lecture is not a device checkoff.
按训练稳定器材、移除驱动器及针芯，立即安全容纳锐器，再用受保护、已预充接头连接。一般讲课不等于器材技能签核。

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:12.672
Use the actual placement and patency checks, including aspiration where specified, site observation and response to the approved test. No single cue proves every later infusion safe.
采用实际位置及通畅检查，包括有规定时回抽、观察局部及获准测试的反应。任何一个提示都不能证明之后所有输注安全。

00:20:12.672 --> 00:20:24.840
Observe for soft-tissue swelling, leakage, unexpected pain and distal neurovascular change. Suspected malposition or extravasation is a stop-and-reassess problem.
要观察软组织肿胀、渗漏、异常疼痛及远端神经血管变化。疑似位置错误或外渗，需要停下重评。

00:20:24.840 --> 00:20:34.728
Flow may require the appropriate trained pressure setup, but greater pressure must not be used to overcome a route that may be misplaced or causing tissue injury.
流动可能需要适当受训加压设置，但不能用更大压力强行通过可能错位或造成组织损伤的通路。

00:20:34.728 --> 00:20:43.680
Reconfirm before further administration and after moving the person. A stable-looking hub is not sufficient evidence of safe delivery.
进一步给入前及搬患者后都应再确认。接头看起来稳定，不是安全送入的充分证据。

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:54.864
An IO insertion and an IO infusion can hurt differently. A patient who responds to pain needs an appropriate plan even if they cannot carry on a normal conversation.
IO置入和输注可造成不同疼痛。能对痛刺激作反应者，即使不能正常交谈，也需要适当疼痛方案。

00:20:54.864 --> 00:21:09.168
Current PR twelve places conscious-patient lidocaine administration with ACP or a PCP under direction of an on-scene ACP. Do not infer an independent PCP anesthetic permission from a classroom case.
当前PR12把清醒患者利多卡因给入交由ACP，或在现场ACP指导下的PCP实施。不能从课堂案例推断PCP有独立麻醉权限。

00:21:09.168 --> 00:21:22.680
Verify the actual medicine formulation and order, relevant contraindications, extension volume and delivery timing. A dose sitting in the extension has not necessarily reached the medullary space.
须核实际药物制剂、医嘱、相关禁忌、延长管容积及给入时间。药还在延长管内，不一定已到骨髓空间。

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:34.152
Continue monitoring and communicate inadequate pain relief or complications. Do not improvise an extra dose or copy a manufacturer's optional regimen into a local order.
应继续监测，并沟通镇痛不足或并发症。不能自行追加剂量，也不能把制造商可选方案当成本地医嘱。

00:21:34.152 --> 00:21:47.640
The saved school Wednesday case says zero point five milligrams per kilogram over sixty seconds. That wording is retained as a source discrepancy, not silently rewritten as if the school said something else.
学校存档周三案例写每千克0.5毫克、60秒给入。这里保留为来源差异，不会悄悄改写成学校原本说了别的。

00:21:47.640 --> 00:22:01.344
Current PR twelve states forty milligrams for the conscious adult, slowly over one hundred and twenty seconds, then a sixty-second dwell before the subsequent specified flush, under its stated clinical authority.
当前PR12对清醒成人列40毫克，缓慢120秒给入，再等待60秒，随后按所列方法冲管，并须满足规定临床权限。

00:22:01.344 --> 00:22:12.624
Its child weight-based statement does not erase the PCP under-twelve cannulation prohibition. Adult versus child wording and on-scene supervision remain separate requirements.
其儿童体重剂量表述不会取消PCP未满12岁禁止置管。成人儿童用词和现场督导，仍是各自独立要求。

00:22:12.624 --> 00:22:25.248
For a station, explicitly identify the discrepancy and ask the instructor for the current approved sequence. Do not invent a hybrid dose, sixty-second rate or extra-dose schedule.
站点中应明确指出差异，请教师确认当前获准流程。不能自创混合剂量、60秒速度或追加剂量安排。

00:22:25.248 --> 00:22:36.456
Protect the catheter during movement and keep the site/limb accessible to reassessment. A displacement can change delivery from medullary circulation to soft tissue.
搬动时保护导管，并保持局部和肢体可评估。移位可让原本进入骨髓循环的液体改为进入软组织。

00:22:36.456 --> 00:22:49.224
Assess pain, swelling, leakage and distal function. Increasing tissue tension or neurovascular concern requires urgent appropriate action, not a tighter wrap and more pressure.
应评疼痛、肿胀、渗漏及远端功能。组织张力增加或神经血管担忧，需要紧急适当处理，不是包更紧、压更大。

00:22:49.224 --> 00:23:00.576
Record the device/site, collective attempts, time, exact medicines/fluids and response. Report partial delivery or a failed route truthfully.
记录器材、部位、集体次数、时间、确切药液及反应。如实报告部分给入或通路失败。

00:23:00.576 --> 00:23:11.880
Use the actual clinical plan for ongoing access and removal. A manufacturer's maximum dwell time is not a reason to retain an unnecessary or compromised route.
续用和拔除应依实际照护方案。厂商最长留置时间，不是保留无必要或受损通路的理由。

00:23:11.880 --> 00:23:23.544
This original scenario follows the school learning objective without copying its patient. A forty-three-year-old has prolonged vomiting, poor intake, weakness and low blood pressure.
本原创情境遵循学校学习目标，但不照抄其患者：43岁，长时间呕吐、摄入少、无力及低血压。

00:23:23.544 --> 00:23:35.688
Assess immediate threats and ask what else could this be. Volume loss may be important, but other causes, ongoing losses, medicines and the actual response must be considered.
先评即时威胁，并问还可能是什么。失液可能重要，但还须考虑其他原因、持续丢失、药物及真实反应。

00:23:35.688 --> 00:23:48.672
If indicated access is difficult, improve site/device planning, seek help and reassess priorities. Two failures alone do not meet the restricted awake-patient PCP IO pathway.
有指征的通路困难时，应改善部位及器材规划、求助并重评优先事项。两次失败本身不能满足清醒者PCP受限IO路径。

00:23:48.672 --> 00:24:00.288
Under an authorized plan, evaluate every intervention against the expected benefit and new harm. Report the patient and access status, not just that you eventually got a line.
在获准方案内，每项干预都应比较预期益处和新伤害。应报告患者及通路状态，不能只说最后终于扎上。

00:24:00.288 --> 00:24:11.160
Explain the clinical indication and the ongoing patient concern. A receiving clinician needs to know why the route was established and whether that reason still applies.
要解释临床适应证及患者当前问题。接收者需要知道为什么建立通路，以及这个理由是否仍然存在。

00:24:11.160 --> 00:24:24.504
State the actual site/device, insertion time, attempts and any difficulty or modification. For IO, communicate the actual supervision and pain-management plan as relevant.
应报告真实部位、器材、置入时间、次数及困难或改动。IO相关时，还应交代实际督导和疼痛管理方案。

00:24:24.504 --> 00:24:36.384
Report exact products, concentrations, amounts and rates, including partial administration and relevant tubing residual. A prepared amount is not always the delivered amount.
须报告确切产品、浓度、量及速度，包括部分给入和相关管内残余。准备量不一定等于真正送入量。

00:24:36.384 --> 00:24:47.928
Close with response, complications, current patency and the next care plan. Complete the clinical record and required incident reporting without disguising uncertainty.
最后交代反应、并发症、当前通畅情况及后续方案。如实完成临床及规定事件记录，不能掩盖不确定性。

00:24:47.928 --> 00:25:41.616
Compare the actual reference entries rather than silently harmonizing them. This PHARM copy lists serum potassium 3.6-5.4 mEq/L, sodium 135-145 mEq/L, total calcium 8.8-10.4 mg/dL, magnesium 1.46-2.68 mEq/L and chloride 98-106 mEq/L. The separately assigned FON table uses some different intervals. The PHARM phosphate numbers labelled mEq/L remain a unit problem, not a validated equivalent table. For a patient, retain the actual laboratory analyte, specimen, unit and interval; neither textbook defines every clinical action threshold.
应比较真实参考条目，不能悄悄统一。此PHARM副本列血清钾3.6至5.4mEq/L、钠135至145mEq/L、总钙8.8至10.4mg/dL、镁1.46至2.68mEq/L、氯98至106mEq/L；另行指定的FON表部分区间不同。PHARM把磷数字标为mEq/L的单位问题仍保留，不能当已验证等效表。对患者须保留真实化验项目、标本、单位及区间；两本书都不能定义所有临床行动阈值。

00:25:41.616 --> 00:26:26.016
The sodium-potassium pump maintains unequal compartments by using ATP to move three sodium ions out and two potassium ions in per cycle. It is not a measurement of the serum potassium or a guarantee of a normal ECG. In medication history, potassium supplements and potassium-containing salt substitutes can interact importantly with impaired renal excretion, ACE inhibitors, ARBs or potassium-sparing diuretics. Distinguish a prescribed replacement plan from unrestricted supplementation. The source peripheral potassium concentration/rate example is not a universal safe limit and does not override the prohibition on rapid IV potassium push.
钠钾泵每循环利用ATP把三个钠移出、两个钾移入，以维持区室不均；它不是测血钾，也不保证ECG正常。药物史中，补钾及含钾代盐与肾排出受损、ACE抑制剂、ARB或保钾利尿剂相遇可能重要。应区分处方补充计划与不限量补充。来源外周钾浓度及速度例不是普遍安全上限，也不能推翻禁止快速静脉推钾的原则。

00:26:26.016 --> 00:27:10.392
Absorption interactions are part of the assigned mineral teaching. Oral calcium can reduce absorption of levothyroxine and certain tetracycline/quinolone antibiotics; calcium/dairy and oral iron also need product-specific scheduling. The source separately flags magnesium with iron, folic-acid or fibre supplements. Identify the actual formulations and prescribed spacing rather than combining all products together or imposing one interval on every medicine. Ask about nonprescription supplements and antacids. Education about diet or drinking water must remain individualized, especially with renal or heart disease and a fluid restriction.
吸收相互作用属于指定矿物质教学。口服钙可减少左甲状腺素及某些四环素、喹诺酮抗菌药吸收；钙、乳制品与口服铁也需按具体产品安排。来源另提示镁与铁、叶酸或纤维补充剂。应辨实际剂型及处方间隔，不能全部混服，也不能所有药套同一个间隔。要询问非处方补充剂及抗酸剂。饮食或喝水教育需个体化，尤其对肾病、心病及限液患者。

00:27:10.392 --> 00:27:53.592
Connect the PN adverse-effect list to surveillance: catheter infection or thrombosis, fluid overload, glucose disturbances, liver complications and refeeding-related electrolyte shifts are different problems. A concentrated PN product is not an ordinary bag to restart or replace at a guessed rate; a PICC may enter peripherally but have a central tip. Urine sugar alone does not monitor glucose safety, and a printed twelve-hour intake/output example is not the reassessment interval for an acutely deteriorating patient. Report the actual product, access, amount/rate, interruption and new findings to the responsible team.
把肠外营养不良反应表连到监测：导管感染或血栓、容量过多、血糖紊乱、肝并发症及再喂养相关电解质转移，是不同问题。浓缩肠外营养不是可按猜测速度重开或替换的普通液袋；PICC虽由外周进入，尖端却可在中心。尿糖不能单独监测血糖安全，书中12小时出入量例也不是急性恶化患者的复评间隔。应向责任团队报告实际产品、通路、量速、中断及新发现。

00:27:53.592 --> 00:28:33.000
The first assigned cardiac page carries over preload, afterload and contractility before 16.3. Correct its venous-direction shortcut: venoconstriction can mobilize venous blood toward the heart, whereas venodilation can promote pooling; less venoconstriction does not automatically increase preload. Filling pressure and filling volume depend on compliance, and more filling does not always increase useful output in a failing ventricle. Inotropy can be positive or negative. Use these distinctions to explain why pressure improvement alone does not prove a successful fluid intervention.
指定心脏起始页在16.3前承接前负荷、后负荷及收缩性。须修正其静脉方向简化：静脉收缩可动员血回心，静脉扩张可促淤积；较少静脉收缩并不自动增加前负荷。充盈压与充盈容量关系受顺应性影响，衰竭心室多充盈也不总增加有效心排。变力作用可正可负。应据此解释为何血压改善不能单独证明补液成功。

00:28:33.000 --> 00:29:14.688
Read each ECG lead as its own potential-difference view, not a numerical sum of twelve lead traces. Depolarization moving toward a lead positive pole generally produces an upward deflection; vector direction and repolarization conventions matter. P, QRS and T relate to atrial depolarization, ventricular depolarization and ventricular repolarization, not measured flow. The assigned final page includes the Chapter 16 summary and key terms, whose artery/vein wording still needs the direction-versus-oxygen correction. A named normal rhythm does not prove normal perfusion or exclude ischemia.
每个ECG导联是自身的电位差视角，不是把十二条记录数值相加。除极朝导联正极运动一般产生向上偏转，但矢量方向及复极规则仍重要。P、QRS、T分别联系房除极、室除极及室复极，不是测得的血流。指定末页包括第16章总结和关键词，其中动静脉措辞仍须按方向与含氧区别来修正。节律名称正常，不证明灌注正常，也不排除缺血。

00:29:14.688 --> 00:30:01.800
The literal last page, printed 140, already starts 5.4: its objectives introduce vitamins/minerals, chelation, complementary therapies, interactions and patient education; the visible body distinguishes water-soluble from fat-soluble vitamins. Water-soluble vitamins generally need ongoing intake and renal handling matters, whereas fat-soluble vitamins can accumulate and cause toxicity. Do not turn this into a rule that every water-soluble vitamin has no storage: vitamin B12 has substantial body stores. Malabsorption, losses and increased requirements can matter. The following detailed vitamin table and chelator sections are not inside this assigned page span.
字面指定末页印刷140已开始5.4：其目标介绍维生素、矿物质、螯合、辅助疗法、相互作用及患者教育，可见正文区分水溶性与脂溶性维生素。水溶性通常需持续摄入且受肾处理影响，脂溶性可蓄积并致毒；但不能说所有水溶性维生素都不储存，B12就有相当体内储备。吸收不良、丢失及需求增加均可相关。后续详细维生素表及螯合剂各节不在此指定页段内。

00:30:01.800 --> 00:30:45.576
The literal first page also completes the preceding respiratory-specimen topic. Collection technique, specimen quality, contamination, timing, prior medicines and transport/storage can change sputum or nasal/throat results. Older adults may have a weaker cough, thicker secretions or difficulty understanding instructions; adapt communication and assistance without forcing an unsafe collection. A swab must match the intended test. A poorly collected or late specimen can mislead even when the laboratory method works correctly. This carryover is reading context, not an additional assessed Week 3 sputum station.
字面起始页还完成前面的呼吸标本主题。采集技术、标本质量、污染、时机、既往药物及转运储存，都可改变痰或鼻咽结果。老年人可能咳嗽弱、分泌物稠，或难理解指示，应调整沟通协助，不能强行不安全采集。拭子必须匹配检验。即使化验方法正常，采集差或延迟的标本仍可误导。这是承接的阅读背景，不是新增第3周痰采样考核站。

00:30:45.576 --> 00:31:28.080
A vacuum collection tube draws blood because its internal pressure is lower; the holder supports the compatible collection system. The source photograph uses lavender for a CBC and red for serum testing, but the actual additive, test, fill and mixing instructions control selection, not colour alone. Preserve patient identification at the bedside and do not transfer blood between tubes to repair a wrong collection. Its statement about whole blood being a fixed fraction of extracellular fluid also needs caution: plasma is extracellular, while red-cell water is intracellular; whole blood and plasma are not the same compartment.
真空采血管以较低内压吸入血液，管架支持相容采集系统。来源照片以紫管示CBC、红管示血清检验，但选管应依真实添加剂、检验、装量及混匀说明，不只看颜色。床旁须保留患者身份核对，不能把血倒来倒去补救错误采集。来源把全血列成细胞外液固定比例也需谨慎：血浆在细胞外，红细胞内的水在细胞内，全血与血浆不是同一区室。

00:31:28.080 --> 00:32:13.680
Read the CVAD diagrams as separate channels, not as a guarantee of compatible medicines. Its illustrated triple-lumen table uses proximal/middle 18-gauge and distal 16-gauge channels, with differing assigned uses; another catheter can have a different layout. The sampling table includes examples of 10-mL syringes, 10-20 mL saline flushes and 2-25 mL discarded blood. These depend on the device, dead space, test, patient and approved method, not a universal sequence to apply to a child or unfamiliar line. Protect critical infusions, use approved aseptic access and avoid unnecessary blood loss.
把CVAD图读成分开的通道，不是保证药物相容。其三腔示例表使用近端、中间18G，远端16G，并分配不同用途；另一导管可有不同布局。采样表含10mL注射器、10至20mL盐水冲洗及2至25mL弃血等例，取决于器材、死腔、检验、患者及获准方法，不是套给儿童或陌生管路的统一顺序。须保护关键输注，按获准无菌连接，并避免无谓失血。

00:32:13.680 --> 00:32:56.496
For the capillary-site drawing, distinguish an adult fingertip example from infant heel sampling. The source infant example uses the medial or lateral plantar heel surface and avoids the centre and posterior curve. Use the actual age-appropriate, depth-limited device and authorized procedure; an illustrated site is not approval for every glucose meter. Excessive squeezing can dilute the sample with tissue fluid or cause hemolysis. Follow actual cleaning/drying and first-drop instructions for the test, record the site/time/result and respond to a critically ill patient without waiting through an unnecessary sampling ritual.
毛细血管部位图须区分成人指端例与婴儿足跟采样。来源婴儿例选足跟足底内外侧，避中心及后侧弧面。应使用真实年龄适配、限制深度的器材及获准流程；图上有某部位，不表示每个血糖仪都批准在那里用。过度挤压可混入组织液或致溶血。清洁干燥及首滴处理按真实检验要求，记部位、时间和结果；患者危重时，不能为不必要采样仪式等待。

00:32:56.496 --> 00:33:44.496
The assigned IV-drug examples span antibiotics, analgesics, emergency medicines, chemotherapy and immunoglobulin. Examples include vancomycin, ketorolac, fentanyl, naloxone and seizure medicines; they illustrate different indications and monitoring, not a new PCP drug list. Alteplase is a tissue plasminogen activator, not a second unrelated drug beside tPA. IVIG is an antibody product, not an antibiotic. Bioavailability is the fraction reaching systemic circulation, not the speed of effect, and IV delivery does not make every medicine safe as a rapid push. Identify an existing infusion by actual name, concentration, route and order.
指定静脉药例涵盖抗菌药、镇痛药、急救药、化疗及免疫球蛋白，如万古霉素、酮咯酸、芬太尼、纳洛酮及抗抽搐药；这些说明不同指征和监测，不是新增PCP药单。阿替普酶属于组织型纤溶酶原激活剂，不是与tPA并列的另一种无关药。IVIG是抗体产品，不是抗菌药。生物利用度是进入体循环的比例，不是起效速度；静脉给入也不使所有药都能快速推注。应以真实药名、浓度、途径及医嘱辨既有输注。

00:33:44.496 --> 00:34:33.000
Read the hardware labels, not a memorized appearance. Lower gauge numbers mean larger internal diameter for otherwise comparable catheters; the source wording later reverses larger and smaller gauge descriptions. Its macrodrip examples are 10, 15 or 20 gtt/mL and microdrip 60 gtt/mL; use the package value. In the source primary/secondary arrangement, bag height and a suitable backcheck valve help select flow, but compatibility, residual tubing volume and the actual flush plan determine delivery. A smart or syringe pump still needs the correct product, syringe, settings and patient/site checks; it is not a universal interaction detector.
应读器材标签，不靠背外观。在其他条件可比时，G数越小，导管内径越大；来源后文却把较大较小G的描述颠倒。其宏滴例为10、15或20gtt/mL，微滴60gtt/mL，实际须读包装。来源主副管路结构中，袋高及合适单向阀帮助选择流向，但相容性、残留管内容积及真实冲洗方案决定给入。智能泵或注射泵仍要核产品、注射器、设定及患者部位；它不是通用相互作用检测器。

00:34:33.000 --> 00:35:16.968
Secure the catheter without hiding the assessment site or creating constriction. The source injury story illustrates why obscured swelling and delayed recognition can cause lasting harm. Keep the skin, insertion site and distal function inspectable according to the actual dressing/device plan, and respond to pain or new swelling rather than trusting that fluid is still running. The distal-first principle preserves options; its phrase about leaking into the intravascular space is misleading when describing infiltration into surrounding tissue. A vein map or near-infrared locator aids location, not proof of successful intravascular placement or freedom from nerve/artery injury.
固定导管时不能遮住需评估的部位，也不能勒紧。来源损伤故事说明，看不见肿胀并延迟识别可留下长期伤害。应按真实敷料器材计划使皮肤、穿刺点及远端功能可评估；出现痛或新肿要应对，不能因液体仍在滴就放心。远端先行用于保留选择；来源描述周围组织浸润时写成漏入血管内，措辞误导。静脉图或近红外定位可辅助找点，不证明已经在血管内，也不保证避开神经动脉损伤。

00:35:16.968 --> 00:35:59.400
Original linked encounter: an adult receiving a home infusion reports new arm pain and swelling, and a critical laboratory result was drawn from the infusing side. Assess and support the patient, stop the implicated delivery appropriately, protect the site and obtain the product/device-specific care plan. The sample may be contaminated or hemolyzed, but that possibility does not prove the dangerous result false or justify ignoring deterioration. Communicate the source of the sample, actual infusion and new findings; arrange appropriate confirmation while immediate care continues. Do not force-flush the line to make it look patent.
原创串联场景：家中输注成人出现新手臂痛肿，危急化验结果的样本又来自输注侧。应评估支持患者，适当停相关给入，保护局部，并取得产品及器材专门照护方案。标本可能被污染或溶血，但这种可能不证明危险结果一定是假，也不能忽视恶化。应沟通取样来源、真实输注及新发现，在即时照护继续时安排适当确认。不能为显得通畅而强冲管。

00:35:59.400 --> 00:36:44.832
The literal printed 1022 page is a hearing/balance page, not section 18.3. Interpret its tuning-fork drawing carefully: Rinne compares air with bone conduction; air greater than bone can be normal or sensorineural loss, whereas bone greater than air supports a conductive component. Weber at the midline normally remains central, or may remain central with equal bilateral loss; in a unilateral pattern it tends toward the conductive-loss ear or away from the sensorineural-loss ear. The picture label normal on one side is not a rule that normal hearing lateralizes. Formal audiology may be needed; this is not a new Week 3 assessed tuning-fork station.
字面印刷1022页是听力及平衡页，不是18.3。须谨慎读音叉图：Rinne比较气导与骨导，气导大于骨导可为正常或感音神经性损失，骨导大于气导支持传导性成分。Weber置中时，正常通常居中，对称双侧损失也可居中；单侧模式则倾向传导性损失耳，或远离感音神经性损失耳。图把某侧标正常，不表示正常听力必侧化。可能需正式听力学检查；这不是新增第3周音叉考核站。

00:36:44.832 --> 00:37:27.288
The same page describes balance observation, a Romberg comparison, facial-nerve findings and the start of validating/documenting findings. A positive Romberg classically means relative stability with eyes open but marked loss of stability after closing them; it does not by itself diagnose an inner-ear disease. Instability with eyes open is already abnormal, not reassurance because the book calls the comparison negative. Guard against falling and do not provoke the test in someone unsafe to stand. Record actual gait/balance and facial asymmetry with the rest of the neurological assessment rather than labeling every dizzy patient a benign ear problem.
同页还描述平衡观察、Romberg比较、面神经发现，以及核实记录开头。典型Romberg阳性指睁眼相对稳、闭眼后明显失稳，不能单独诊断内耳病。睁眼已不稳本来就是异常，不能因书把比较称阴性就放心。须防跌倒，不能让不适合站立的人勉强做。应把真实步态平衡及面部不对称连到其余神经评估记录，不能把所有头晕者标成良性耳病。

00:37:27.288 --> 00:37:38.232
Without reading, explain the access indication, the patient risk and the alternative route you considered. State why hospital convenience or practice alone is not enough.
不看课件，解释通路适应证、患者风险及考虑过的替代途径，并说明为什么医院方便或练手本身都不够。

00:37:38.232 --> 00:37:48.768
On the model, lay out the full equipment and describe the protected parts and actual device transitions. A partner should be able to identify a contamination break.
在模型上摆出完整器材，描述受保护部位及真实器材转换。同伴应能指出无菌中断点。

00:37:48.768 --> 00:37:59.448
Describe the response to a failed attempt, swelling during a flush and a new breathing problem during fluid. None is solved by blindly increasing force or rate.
说明如何响应尝试失败、冲管时肿胀，以及补液中出现新呼吸问题。三者都不能通过盲目加力或加速解决。

00:37:59.448 --> 00:38:11.400
Finish by distinguishing the school IO scenario from current PR twelve and by using the three post-intervention questions. These are preparation, not a signed practical qualification.
最后区分学校IO情境与当前PR12，并使用干预后三问。这些用于准备，不代表已经签核技能资质。
